Provide a function using either merge sort or heap sort algorithm that can sort a large, randomized array of integer values. In addition, the function has to handle real-time addition and deletion of elements in the array while maintaining the sorted order of the array. This implies that your sort algorithm needs to be online. Validate this with a series of tests that add and remove elements at various points in the array.

```python
import bisect

class OnlineSorter:
    def __init__(self):
        self.sorted_array = []

    def insert(self, value):
        bisect.insort(self.sorted_array, value)

    def delete(self, value):
        index = bisect.bisect_left(self.sorted_array, value)
        if [MASK]:
            self.sorted_array.pop(index)

    def get_sorted_array(self):
        return self.sorted_array
```

